<title>CHINA: FIRST SHANGHAI BUYS 16.7 PCT OF RBI.</title>
<headline>FIRST SHANGHAI BUYS 16.7 PCT OF RBI.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>RBI Holdings Ltd said on Thursday it had agreed to place 51.21 million new shares, or 16.66 percent of its enlarged share capital, to a third party First Shanghai Investments Ltd at HK$1.50 per share.</p>
<p>On completion of the deal, shareholding of RBI's chairman and controlling shareholder Yip Yun Kuen will be diluted to 35.8 percent from 42.96 percent, RBI said in a statement.</p>
<p>The toy maker said First Shanghai would hold the stake for long term investment purposes.</p>
<p>RBI said the net proceeds of HK$77 million would be used for the expansion of production capacities and for working capital.</p>
<p>Trading in RBI shares resumed on Thursday after a one-day suspension. Its shares gained HK$0.34 or 18.78 percent to HK$2.15 at midday.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6370</p>
